658 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 402 0 R
/E (The existing dog adoption process often relies on manual records, spreadsheets, phone calls, and emails to manage dog profiles, adopter details, and adoption applications. This makes it difficult to maintain accurate information, process applications quickly, and monitor adoption progress. Therefore, a centralized Dog Adoption Management System is needed to automate adoption activities, improve communication, protect user data, and ensure efficient coordination between adopters, shelters/rescuers, and administrators.)
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
659 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 402 0 R
/T (Key Pain Points)
/E (Key Pain Points)
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
660 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 2702 0 R
/E (Data Duplication: Maintaining records across multiple spreadsheets and documents can lead to duplicate or inconsistent information.)
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
661 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 2703 0 R
/E (Delayed Approvals: Manual verification of adopters, shelters, dog listings, and applications can slow down the adoption process.)
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
662 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 2704 0 R
/E (Lack of Real-Time Visibility: Users may find it difficult to track application status, dog availability, and adoption progress.)
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
663 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 2705 0 R
/E (Manual Reporting and Follow-Ups: Preparing adoption reports and remembering follow-up dates require extra time and effort.)
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
664 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 2706 0 R
/E (Insufficient Access Control: Without role-based permissions, sensitive adopter information may be exposed to unauthorized users.)
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [11]
>>
endobj
